  <movement-title>Shalom</movement-title>
  <identification>
    <creator type="lyricist">Ancient Hebrew benediction
English text by Wayne Hooper, 1974 (1920-   )</creator>
    <creator type="composer">Irregular
Accomp. by Melvin West, 1984 (1930-   )</creator>
    <rights>Words copyright © 1974 by Wayne Hooper. Arrangement copyright © 1984 by Melvin West.
Alternate version from Chansons de Notre Chalet, copyright 1957 by Cooperative Recreation Service,
Inc., Delaware, Ohio.
The word “Shalom” has a triple meaning: hello, farewell, and peace, with special overtones of loving
concern and sincere caring for each other.
At the beginning of a meeting or as an expression of fellowship during a meeting, change text to “As
we meet again.”
SENTENCES AND RESPONSES</rights>
