  <credit page="1">
    <credit-type>rights</credit-type>
    <credit-words default-x="725.0" default-y="175" justify="center" font-size="7.5" font-weight="normal">Words copyright © 1974 by Wayne Hooper. Arrangement copyright © 1984 by Melvin West.
Alternate version from Chansons de Notre Chalet, copyright 1957 by Cooperative Recreation Service,
Inc., Delaware, Ohio.
The word “Shalom” has a triple meaning: hello, farewell, and peace, with special overtones of loving
concern and sincere caring for each other.
At the beginning of a meeting or as an expression of fellowship during a meeting, change text to “As
we meet again.”
SENTENCES AND RESPONSES</credit-words>
